  "intro": "Kyoto was chosen as Japan's imperial seat in 794, when it was called Heian-kyō, and it stayed the capital until the move to Tokyo in 1869. Today it is a city of about 1.4 million people that still holds roughly 2,000 temples and shrines, from the gold-covered Kinkaku-ji to the torii tunnels of Fushimi Inari. Seventeen of its historic monuments were listed together as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1994.",
